With `--additional-axioms`, a lambda without a reads clause whose body does not observe the heap or allocation is checked well-formed in every good heap without assuming its parameters allocated, and the calls in its body are then permitted to unfold wherever the lambda is used. This restores, for such lambdas, facts that the finite-support and function-value allocation repairs had guarded: for example `(a: int) => 7 - Idx(a)` is again an `int -> nat`, and a family `(o: nat -> int) => F(o)` unfolds at a quantified `o`.
